1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:12,905
By 1972, Cybersyn had a network: Chile's telex lines, being extended to every factory the state ran, along a country more than four thousand kilometres long.

2
00:00:14,605 --> 00:00:18,166
Some managers were won over by the offer of a free telex.

3
00:00:19,466 --> 00:00:25,177
But the software could only warn about a factory if it had that factory's own numbers, from that day.

4
00:00:26,677 --> 00:00:32,865
A figure from anywhere else would mislead it: last month's, or a guess made in an office in Santiago.

5
00:00:34,365 --> 00:00:39,308
Then a bad day could look normal, and a mill short of cotton could wait for help that never came.

6
00:00:41,008 --> 00:00:43,418
Each number had to come from where it was made.

7
00:00:44,918 --> 00:00:50,359
So each factory sent its own numbers by telex, once a day, from the factory itself.

8
00:00:52,059 --> 00:00:56,198
It wasn't easy: the team had to keep reminding managers to send them.

9
00:00:57,698 --> 00:01:02,909
But now each number had one place where it was born: the factory that made what it counted.

10
00:01:04,409 --> 00:01:09,007
What Santiago read was a copy of what that factory had sent, the same day.

11
00:01:10,507 --> 00:01:12,850
The statistics before had taken six months.

12
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:18,157
At the utility, Inés finds a fact that's born in two places.

13
00:01:19,457 --> 00:01:27,499
When a family signs up for a new home, billing creates a premise for it. When the home is connected, the network map creates a service point.

14
00:01:29,199 --> 00:01:35,031
Last year, 214 of 1,160 new homes were created twice.

15
00:01:42,531 --> 00:01:44,826
Take a new home at 14 Quarry Lane.

16
00:01:46,526 --> 00:01:54,852
In March the family signed up. The home had no network ID yet, so billing created a premise of its own, from the address on their form.

17
00:01:56,752 --> 00:02:05,574
In April the network team connected it, and the network map created its service point, at Lot 14, Quarry Lane: the builder's name for the plot.

18
00:02:07,474 --> 00:02:13,097
Customer service copied billing's premise. The outage system copied the network's service point.

19
00:02:14,997 --> 00:02:17,373
In June, the power went out on their street.

20
00:02:19,073 --> 00:02:23,289
The outage system saw the cut at the service point, but no account was on it.

21
00:02:24,989 --> 00:02:31,301
When the family called, customer service found no cut at their address, and told them to call an electrician.

22
00:02:33,201 --> 00:02:35,955
And Grace's measure counted no customer there.

23
00:02:39,255 --> 00:02:44,393
Every fact has a place where it's born: the one system where it's created, and corrected.

24
00:02:46,293 --> 00:02:51,944
DAMA calls it the system of record. Every other system that holds the fact holds a copy.

25
00:02:54,044 --> 00:03:00,408
To find each fact's home, Inés draws what each system does with each thing: creates it, or copies it.

26
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:05,572
Where a row has one "creates", the fact has a home.

27
00:03:07,472 --> 00:03:15,877
Where it has two, it's born twice: the connection point, in billing and in the network map, and the customer, in billing and in customer service.

28
00:03:19,577 --> 00:03:25,855
So Inés proposes a home for the connection point, and its owner, Grace, agrees: the network map.

29
00:03:27,755 --> 00:03:34,400
From now on, only the network map creates a connection point, with its ID, as soon as a connection is planned.

30
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:43,173
Billing no longer makes its own. It asks the network team for one, and copies it, ID and all, the same day.

31
00:03:45,273 --> 00:03:48,883
The account's home is billing, and its owner is the head of retail.

32
00:03:50,783 --> 00:03:56,623
One fact, one home, one owner. A copy can be read anywhere, but it's corrected only at home.

33
00:04:00,523 --> 00:04:06,502
Each copy keeps a line back to where it was born: which system, which record, and when it was copied.

34
00:04:08,202 --> 00:04:09,692
That line is its lineage.

35
00:04:11,392 --> 00:04:18,765
In July, the network team corrected the address to the plot's street number, 14 Quarry Lane, at home in the network map.

36
00:04:20,665 --> 00:04:23,348
By the next morning, every copy said the same.

37
00:04:25,248 --> 00:04:34,259
Grace's measure has lineage too: each interruption it counts traces to a record in the outage system, and each customer to an account in billing.

38
00:04:37,359 --> 00:04:41,492
Now, back to the cut. Each one is recorded by more than one system.

39
00:04:43,192 --> 00:04:47,533
The meter's "power off" event is born in meter data: what the meter saw.

40
00:04:49,233 --> 00:04:53,610
The family's call is born in customer service: what a person told us.

41
00:04:55,310 --> 00:05:01,997
The interruption is born in the outage system: the cut as Grace's team defines it, from its start to its end.

42
00:05:03,897 --> 00:05:08,295
They aren't three copies of one fact. They're three facts, each with its own home.

43
00:05:10,395 --> 00:05:16,673
The outage system reads the other two as evidence, and its record is the one Grace's measure counts.

44
00:05:20,173 --> 00:05:22,689
Some facts can't be born in only one place.

45
00:05:23,789 --> 00:05:30,066
A customer can start in billing, signing up, or in customer service, calling before they've signed anything.

46
00:05:31,366 --> 00:05:38,007
Both have to create one. Then the work is to know when two records are the same person, and which value wins.

47
00:05:39,507 --> 00:05:43,931
That's master data, and the series The same one, everywhere takes it from here.

48
00:05:45,431 --> 00:05:52,080
On the data practice on the map, each data object now names its home, and each copy has a line back to it.

49
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:02,614
In Chile, each number was born in its factory, and sent from there once a day.

50
00:06:03,914 --> 00:06:07,269
Santiago read copies, and knew where each one came from.

51
00:06:08,769 --> 00:06:14,455
At the utility, each fact now has one home and one owner, and every copy a line back to it.

52
00:06:15,955 --> 00:06:23,264
In October, when the power went out on Quarry Lane again, the family's call found the cut, and Grace's measure counted them.

53
00:06:24,964 --> 00:06:28,033
Since July, no new home has been created twice.

54
00:06:29,533 --> 00:06:35,936
But a fact doesn't stay at home. A meter reading replaced in the network has to reach billing. How does it travel?
